Start();
include(unitTests);
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking;
include("IncantForms/WorkingOn/parser");
define
    llSay code={
        v := tell(argument);
        m := *v["matched"]; c := *v["consumed"];
        cerr "LL-DRIVE " argument " matched= " m " consumed= " c:;
        rp = 0;
        if *v["reply"];     rp = 1;
        if rp == 1;     labelSpans(*v["reply"]);
        if rp == 0;     cerr "SPAN (no reply)":;
        };
    ;
register(LeafLab);
define
    LlWord=[a-z]+;
    ;
define
    LlOUT isRule lp="(" kw="let" LlWord rp=")";
    ;
search GroupFields UnitTests Utilities LeafLab list;
cerr "--- OLD ROAD":;
llSay("LlOUT (letabc)");
parser(LlOUT);
cerr "--- NEW ROAD":;
llSay("LlOUT (letabc)");
llSay("LlOUT (letxyzw)");
cerr "LEAFLABEL SENTINEL":;
stop();

leafLabelT -- A NEW-ROAD LEAF'S LABEL, READ BACK BY VALUE (SEQ 302 R1; 1.2f leans on this row).

LlOUT's terms lp="(", kw="let" and rp=")" are LABELLED LITERALS: parser() installs them as new-road parseString leaves,
which since 1.2c keep their label in a local and hand it to exitFromParse, where it attaches under LlOUT's label.
labelSpans prints the reply tree with each node's tag and the span it covers, so the row reads each leaf's TAG and
TEXT by value -- lp [(], kw [let], rp [)]. LlWord is a set FIELD; it runs the old road inside the new-road body
(driveStep's old-road attach), so it is the control: present under the H7 as well as without it. The old road runs
first (parser() is one-way) as the comparison.

⚠ WHY LITERALS, measured 2026-10-05: a labelled inline SET (wd=[a-z]+) and a set field both kept their labels when the
leaves handed the exit no label -- they do not take the new-road leaf path -- so a set-only fixture certified nothing.
The labelled literals' labels vanish under that H7: a wrong VALUE, not a crash.

Before this row the leaf-label handoff's only witness was leafClassT, which crashed when the label went missing.

labelSpans is a printer beside labelTree (measure.twk): labelTree prints tags only, and a kant subscript could not reach
the child label of tell's reply (`*lt["wd"]` and `*lt[1]` both read nothing).
